The CPU sampler's stable radix ordering was independently implemented in Rust,
inspired by DeepInfer's radix-based vocabulary filtering in
 deepinfer/model_executor/layers/tilelang_ops/cuda/fused_sample.py.
No DeepInfer CUDA/TileLang kernel is copied or linked.

The bounded, double-buffered HYT resident loader was independently implemented
in Rust, informed by DeepInfer PR #52 (double-buffered pinned weight loading):
  https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepInfer/pull/52
  reviewed head: 2b30706c94998f6887dce525f9aa9f575d6912c3
It uses Hayate's existing validation, positional reads and CUDA runtime.

Build dependencies fetched separately by engines/hayate/scripts/fetch-third-party.sh:
  FlashInfer (Apache-2.0), including its pinned CUTLASS (BSD-3-Clause).
  Their upstream license notices remain in the fetched sources.

Native Kogarashi GGML compatibility:
  Q4_K and Q6_K block layouts and decoder formulas follow llama.cpp / ggml.
  Upstream: https://gitlab.com/agentionai-group/llama.cpp
  Reference revision: 9aa51ce4fdd3435a91531ffe16a17414ccc6dc6f
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors.
  License: licenses/llama.cpp-MIT.
  The native decoder does not link the reference backend. The reference
  backend and its MTP patch remain separately available for differential tests.

